Subject: [EXPERIMENT] wifi: brcmfmac: propagate transport failure from netdev open

The post-S3 Wi-Fi enable trace records toe_ol timing out with -EIO,
followed immediately by brcmf_netdev_open returning success. The retained
cfg->dongle_up state lets cfg80211_up skip firmware initialization.

Keep optional TOE firmware rejection (-EBADE) compatible with the successful
awake toggle. Return transport errors instead of advertising successful open.
This addresses false success only. It does not repair the stalled firmware or
make the later Wi-Fi watchdog reset safe for its Bluetooth sibling.
Not hardware tested; no deployment or complete suspend-fix claim.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -604,6 +604,7 @@
 	struct brcmf_pub *drvr = ifp->drvr;
 	struct brcmf_bus *bus_if = drvr->bus_if;
 	u32 toe_ol;
+	int err;
 
 	brcmf_dbg(TRACE, "Enter, bsscfgidx=%d\n", ifp->bsscfgidx);
 
@@ -616,8 +617,13 @@
 	atomic_set(&ifp->pend_8021x_cnt, 0);
 
 	/* Get current TOE mode from dongle */
-	if (brcmf_fil_iovar_int_get(ifp, "toe_ol", &toe_ol) >= 0
-	    && (toe_ol & TOE_TX_CSUM_OL) != 0)
+	err = brcmf_fil_iovar_int_get(ifp, "toe_ol", &toe_ol);
+	/* FWIL maps a firmware rejection to EBADE. Other failures do not
+	 * establish a working transport, even though TOE is optional.
+	 */
+	if (err < 0 && err != -EBADE)
+		return err;
+	if (!err && (toe_ol & TOE_TX_CSUM_OL) != 0)
 		ndev->features |= NETIF_F_IP_CSUM;
 	else
 		ndev->features &= ~NETIF_F_IP_CSUM;
